UPDATE public.legal_documents SET
  title = $L$Terms of Use$L$,
  content = $L$<p><strong>Effective date:</strong> 05.03.2026. <strong>Version:</strong> 2.0.</p>

<h2>1. Introduction, parties and acceptance of the Terms</h2>
<p>These Terms are a legal agreement between you and "ANACAN" Məhdud Məsuliyyətli Cəmiyyəti governing your use of the Anacan app. You accept these Terms by giving your active confirmation when creating an account.</p>

<h3>1.1. Parties</h3>
<ul>
<li><strong>Service provider ("Anacan", "we"):</strong> "ANACAN" Məhdud Məsuliyyətli Cəmiyyəti, TIN 1407578211, Şamil Əzizbəyov 150, Republic of Azerbaijan.</li>
<li><strong>User ("you"):</strong> a natural person who creates an account in the Anacan app or uses it.</li>

<li><strong>Single point of contact for authorities and users (DSA, Articles 11–12):</strong> legal@anacan.az. Communication is possible in Azerbaijani, English and Russian.</li>
</ul>

<h3>1.2. What the "Service" is</h3>
<p>The Service covers the Anacan mobile app, website and all of their features:</p>
<ul>
<li>cycle, pregnancy and child development tracking;</li>
<li>informational articles and recommendations;</li>
<li>an artificial intelligence assistant (the "AI assistant");</li>
<li>community: posts, stories, groups and private messaging;</li>
<li>Premium subscription;</li>
<li>offers from brand partners.</li>
</ul>

<h3>1.3. Acceptance of the Terms</h3>
<p>You accept these Terms by ticking the "I accept the Terms of Use" box during registration. The box is not pre-ticked.</p>
<p>The Privacy Policy is not part of these Terms. It explains how we process your personal data, and you review it separately. Consents for health data, marketing and advertising are obtained separately from these Terms, and refusing them does not affect your acceptance of the Terms.</p>
<p>If you do not agree with these Terms, do not use the Service.</p>

<h3>1.4. Age limit</h3>
<p>You must be at least <strong>16 years old</strong> to use the Service. If the law of the country where you live requires a higher age, that age applies.</p>
<p>The following additional safeguards apply to users under 18:</p>
<ul>
<li>the profile is private by default;</li>
<li>they cannot receive private messages from adult users they do not know;</li>
<li>no personalised advertising is shown;</li>
<li>they cannot join groups that are not appropriate for their age.</li>
</ul>
<p>Providing false information about your age is a breach of these Terms.</p>

<h2>2. Account and security</h2>
<p>You are responsible for the activity on your account. You must notify us immediately of any unauthorised use of your account.</p>

<h3>2.1. Creating an account</h3>
<ul>
<li>Each person may create only one personal account.</li>
<li>The information you provide during registration must be accurate.</li>
<li>Creating an account in another person's name without their permission is prohibited.</li>
<li>You may use a nickname, but you may not choose a name that impersonates another real person, a brand or an Anacan employee.</li>
</ul>

<h3>2.2. Account security</h3>
<ul>
<li>Do not share your password with anyone. Anacan employees will never ask for your password.</li>
<li>Where possible, enable two-factor authentication and the app lock (PIN, Face ID, fingerprint).</li>
<li>If you suspect unauthorised use of your account, write immediately to security@anacan.az.</li>
<li>If we detect that the security of your account has been compromised, we may temporarily restrict access and require you to reset your password in order to protect you.</li>
</ul>

<h3>2.3. Shared access</h3>
<p>When you invite a partner or caregiver to your account, only you choose what they will see. You can revoke access at any time. The person you invite is also bound by these Terms.</p>

<h3>2.4. Deleting your account</h3>
<p>You can delete your account at any time under Profile → Settings → Privacy and Data → Delete account. You can export your data before deletion. Detailed information about deletion is provided in the Privacy Policy. Deleting your account does not automatically cancel an App Store or Google Play subscription (see Section 4).</p>

<h2>3. Medical disclaimer and AI assistant</h2>
<p>Anacan is not a medical service, a medical device or a means of contraception. Make decisions about your health together with your doctor.</p>

<h3>3.1. Informational service</h3>
<ul>
<li>The articles, predictions, reminders and AI responses in the app are for general information only.</li>
<li>They are not medical advice, diagnosis or treatment and do not replace a doctor's advice.</li>
<li>Using the Service does not create a doctor–patient relationship between you and Anacan or its employees.</li>
<li>Do not delay or forgo medical advice because of information you have seen in the app.</li>
</ul>

<h3>3.2. Limitations of predictions</h3>
<p>Predictions of menstruation, ovulation, fertile days and the due date are estimates based on the data you enter and on statistical models. Stress, illness, medication, the postpartum period, breastfeeding and hormonal changes affect the accuracy of predictions.</p>
<p><strong>Do not use the predictions as contraception or as a method of preventing pregnancy.</strong> Anacan makes no claim of contraceptive effectiveness.</p>

<h3>3.3. Emergencies</h3>
<p>The app is not intended for emergency medical help. In the following cases, contact emergency services immediately (103 in Azerbaijan, 112 in the EU) or your doctor:</p>
<ul>
<li>heavy bleeding or severe abdominal pain;</li>
<li>during pregnancy: bleeding, leaking fluid, reduced foetal movement, severe headache, visual disturbances or swelling;</li>
<li>high fever, loss of consciousness, shortness of breath;</li>
<li>in a baby: difficulty breathing, refusal to feed, high fever or lethargy;</li>
<li>thoughts of harming yourself or someone else.</li>
</ul>

<h3>3.4. AI assistant</h3>
<p>The AI assistant generates automated responses using artificial intelligence. When you talk to it, you are communicating with an AI system, not with a human.</p>
<ul>
<li>AI responses may be incorrect, incomplete or outdated.</li>
<li>The AI assistant does not diagnose, prescribe medicines or prescribe treatment.</li>
<li>Do not take medicines, change a dose or stop treatment based on AI responses.</li>
<li>Do not use the AI assistant in emergencies (see 3.3).</li>
<li>What you write to the assistant is processed in accordance with the Privacy Policy. Google (Vertex AI, Gemini) does not use this data to train its own models.</li>
<li>The right to use the AI assistant's responses belongs to you. However, we do not guarantee that they do not infringe the rights of others.</li>
</ul>

<h3>3.5. Information in the community</h3>
<p>Opinions, experiences and recommendations shared by other users in the community are their personal views. They are not verified and do not reflect the position of Anacan. A user presenting themselves as a doctor does not prove that they actually are a doctor.</p>

<h2>4. Premium subscription and payments</h2>
<p>The Premium subscription is purchased through the App Store or Google Play, renews automatically until cancelled, and can be cancelled at any time in that store's settings.</p>
<p>Premium can also be purchased on the anacan.az website with a bank card (via Epoint). In this case, your card is stored on the bank's side for automatic renewal (we only see the masked number), the subscription renews at the same price at the end of the period you selected, and it can be cancelled at any time on the "My Premium account" page on the website.</p>

<h3>4.1. Plans and prices</h3>
<ul>
<li>Premium is offered with monthly and annual plans. Current prices are shown in the app before purchase in your local currency, including taxes.</li>
<li>The basic tracking features are available in the free version. Premium provides additional features and removes advertising. The current list of Premium features is shown in the app.</li>
</ul>

<h3>4.2. Payment and automatic renewal</h3>
<ul>
<li>Payment is charged to your App Store or Google Play account when you confirm the purchase. Payment is processed by Apple or Google; we do not see your card details.</li>
<li>Unless the subscription is cancelled at least 24 hours before the end of the current period, it renews automatically for the same term at the current price.</li>
<li>If the price increases, we notify you in advance. Where the store rules require it, the new price applies only after your confirmation.</li>
</ul>

<h3>4.3. Free trial period</h3>
<p>If a free trial is offered, its length is shown before purchase. If you do not cancel at least 24 hours before the trial ends, the paid subscription starts automatically.</p>

<h3>4.4. Cancellation</h3>
<ul>
<li><strong>iOS:</strong> Settings → [your name] → Subscriptions → Anacan → Cancel Subscription.</li>
<li><strong>Android:</strong> Google Play → Profile → Payments and subscriptions → Subscriptions → Anacan → Cancel.</li>
</ul>
<p>When you cancel, Premium remains active until the end of the current paid period.</p>

<h3>4.5. 14-day right of withdrawal for EU, EEA and UK consumers</h3>
<p>If you live in the EU, the EEA or the United Kingdom, you have the right to withdraw from the contract for digital content and services within 14 days of purchase without giving any reason.</p>
<p>For Premium to be activated immediately, we ask for a separate confirmation at the time of purchase: "I want immediate access to Premium and I acknowledge that I lose my right of withdrawal once the supply of digital content has begun." Without this confirmation, your right of withdrawal is preserved.</p>
<p>To withdraw, use the App Store or Google Play refund procedure or write to us at support@anacan.az.</p>

<h3>4.6. Refunds</h3>
<p>Decisions on refunds are mainly made by the App Store and Google Play in accordance with their own rules. This does not limit the rights granted to you by law. If there is a prolonged or serious malfunction of the Service, write to support@anacan.az.</p>

<h3>4.7. Additional terms for Apple users</h3>
<p>These Terms are between you and Anacan only, not with Apple. Anacan, not Apple, is responsible for the app and its content. Apple has no obligation to provide technical support for the app. Claims relating to the app (product liability, legal compliance, consumer protection) are handled by Anacan, not Apple. Anacan, not Apple, is responsible for third-party intellectual property claims. Apple and its subsidiaries are third-party beneficiaries of these Terms and may enforce them against you. You confirm that you do not live in a country subject to a US embargo and that you are not on any US government list of prohibited persons.</p>

<h2>5. Community and user content</h2>
<p>The content you share remains yours. You grant us a limited licence to use it solely to provide the Service, and this licence ends when you delete your account.</p>

<h3>5.1. Community features</h3>
<table>
<thead><tr><th>Feature</th><th>Who can see it</th><th>Special rules</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
<tr><td>Posts</td><td>The audience you choose (everyone, followers, a group)</td><td>The audience of each post is shown on that post</td></tr>
<tr><td>Stories</td><td>The audience you choose</td><td>Not visible to others after 24 hours; only you can see the archive</td></tr>
<tr><td>Groups</td><td>Public groups: everyone; private groups: members</td><td>Group administrators may set their own rules, but these may not fall below these Terms</td></tr>
<tr><td>Private messages</td><td>Only the participants in the conversation</td><td>Moderated on the basis of reports (see 7.7)</td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<p><strong>Anonymous posting.</strong> On some topics you can post anonymously. In an anonymous post, your name is not shown to other users, but the post remains linked to your account and may be seen by moderators if the rules are breached.</p>
<p><strong>Please note.</strong> Health information you share in the community can be seen, saved or screenshotted by other users. Choose what you share with care. Content you share in the community is separate from your cycle and pregnancy records and is your decision to share.</p>

<h3>5.2. Your rights to your content</h3>
<p>You retain all rights to the text, images, videos, stories and messages you share ("User Content").</p>

<h3>5.3. The licence you grant us</h3>
<p>By sharing User Content, you grant Anacan the following licence:</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Scope:</strong> to store the content, process it technically (for example, resize it), display it to the audience you choose and moderate it.</li>
<li><strong>Nature:</strong> non-exclusive, royalty-free, without territorial restriction.</li>
<li><strong>Duration:</strong> until you delete the content or your account. After deletion, it may remain in backups for up to 30 days. In content shared or replied to by someone else, your part is deleted.</li>
<li><strong>Purpose:</strong> solely to provide the Service. Without your separate consent, we do not use your content in Anacan's marketing or advertising, do not give it to brand partners and do not use it to train artificial intelligence models.</li>
<li><strong>Sublicence:</strong> only to technical providers who provide the Service on our behalf (hosting, etc.) and only for the purposes above.</li>
</ul>
<p>Your cycle, pregnancy and child records, as well as what you write to the AI assistant, are not User Content. They are not covered by this licence and are processed only in accordance with the Privacy Policy.</p>

<h3>5.4. Your warranties</h3>
<p>When sharing User Content, you confirm that:</p>
<ul>
<li>you have the right to share this content;</li>
<li>you have obtained the consent of other persons who appear in the content, especially children;</li>
<li>the content does not breach these Terms or the law.</li>
</ul>

<h3>5.5. Photos of children</h3>
<p>Before sharing photos of your child in the community, think about their future privacy. Do not share nude or semi-nude photos of a child, or photos that reveal their school, address or daily route. We may remove such content in order to protect children. Sharing a photo of someone else's child without the consent of that child's parent is prohibited.</p>

<h2>6. Community rules</h2>
<p>The Anacan community is a safe and supportive space for women and parents. The following content and conduct are prohibited; depending on the severity of the breach, the measures in Section 7 are taken.</p>

<h3>6.1. Zero tolerance (immediate account termination)</h3>
<ul>
<li>Any content related to the sexual exploitation or sexualisation of children, and any attempt to establish inappropriate contact with children (grooming). Such content is reported to the competent authorities.</li>
<li>Promotion of terrorism and violent extremism.</li>
<li>Real threats of violence against a specific person.</li>
<li>Human trafficking, buying or selling of children or babies, illegal adoption or surrogacy offers.</li>
<li>Non-consensual sharing of intimate images.</li>
</ul>

<h3>6.2. Prohibited content</h3>
<ul>
<li><strong>Insults and harassment:</strong> insults, humiliation, threats and intimidation, stalking, mocking another person's body, parenting decisions or pregnancy loss.</li>
<li><strong>Hate speech:</strong> attacks based on race, ethnicity, religion, nationality, sex, disability or other protected characteristics.</li>
<li><strong>Self-harm:</strong> content that encourages or shows methods of suicide, self-harm or disordered eating. Seeking support on these topics is not prohibited; we may add support resources to such posts.</li>
<li><strong>Dangerous health misinformation:</strong> calls to refuse proven treatment, to use dangerous "treatment" methods, or to engage in practices that could harm children and pregnant women.</li>
<li><strong>Sale of medicines and medical products:</strong> offers to buy, sell or hand over prescription medicines, medicines for terminating a pregnancy, hormones, breast milk or medical devices.</li>
<li><strong>Disclosure of personal information (doxxing):</strong> sharing another person's address, phone number, workplace, health information or photos without their consent.</li>
<li><strong>Fraud and deception:</strong> scams, fake fundraising, pyramid schemes, posing as a doctor or specialist, impersonating another person.</li>
<li><strong>Sexual content:</strong> pornographic or sexually explicit content. Educational content on reproductive health and breastfeeding is not prohibited.</li>
<li><strong>Graphic violence:</strong> bloody or shocking images without a warning. Sensitive images on childbirth and medical topics may be shared only with a "sensitive content" label.</li>
<li><strong>Intellectual property infringement:</strong> sharing someone else's content without permission.</li>
<li><strong>Illegal content:</strong> other content prohibited by the law of the country where you live or by EU law.</li>
</ul>

<h3>6.3. Prohibited conduct</h3>
<ul>
<li>Spam, mass or automated messages, fake accounts, bots.</li>
<li>Undisclosed advertising: if you post in exchange for payment or gifts from a brand, you must clearly indicate this with the "#ad" or "#collaboration" tag.</li>
<li>Creating a new account to evade moderation.</li>
<li>Abuse of the reporting system (unfounded, mass complaints).</li>
<li>Interfering with the security of the Service, automated collection of data (scraping), reverse engineering the app's code (except where permitted by law).</li>
<li>Asking other users for personal information, money or intimate images outside the community.</li>
</ul>

<h3>6.4. Obligations of group administrators</h3>
<p>Users who create or manage a group:</p>
<ul>
<li>must make efforts to ensure compliance with these Terms in the group;</li>
<li>must state any additional rules clearly in the group description;</li>
<li>must clearly disclose when they direct group members to paid services outside the group;</li>
<li>must report content that breaches the rules to us.</li>
</ul>
<p>Group administrators are not employees or representatives of Anacan.</p>

<h2>7. Moderation, reporting and complaints</h2>
<p>The community is reviewed jointly by our moderators and automated tools. When we make a decision about your content, we tell you the reason, and you can appeal that decision. This section has been prepared in accordance with the EU Digital Services Act (DSA, Regulation 2022/2065).</p>

<h3>7.1. Reporting content that breaches the rules (DSA, Article 16)</h3>
<p>Anyone, including people without an account, can report illegal content or content that breaches these Terms:</p>
<ul>
<li>in the app, using the <strong>"Report"</strong> button next to a post, story, comment, group, profile or message;</li>
<li>for people without an account, via report@anacan.az.</li>
</ul>
<p>A report of illegal content must include:</p>
<ol>
<li>an explanation of why the content is illegal;</li>
<li>the exact location of the content (a link or an in-app report);</li>
<li>your name and e-mail address (except for reports concerning child sexual abuse — these may be submitted anonymously);</li>
<li>a confirmation that you believe in good faith that the information in the report is accurate.</li>
</ol>
<p>We confirm receipt of the report, review it in a timely, objective and impartial manner, and inform you of the decision.</p>

<h3>7.2. How moderation is carried out</h3>
<ul>
<li>Reports are reviewed by human moderators. Moderators are trained on health and child-related topics.</li>
<li>We use automated tools for spam, known illegal images and clear-cut rules. Decisions made by an automated tool that result in an account being terminated are reviewed by a human.</li>
<li>Feed and group recommendations are ranked by an algorithm. The main ranking parameters are: the accounts and groups you follow, your life stage, interactions and the date of the post.</li>
</ul>

<h3>7.3. Measures</h3>
<p>Depending on the severity of the breach, whether it is repeated and the context, one or more of the following measures are applied:</p>
<table>
<thead><tr><th>Measure</th><th>Example case</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
<tr><td>Warning</td><td>First-time, minor breach</td></tr>
<tr><td>Restricting the visibility of content ("sensitive content" label, removal from recommendations)</td><td>Graphic medical image</td></tr>
<tr><td>Removal of content</td><td>Insults, misinformation, sales</td></tr>
<tr><td>Temporary restriction of features (posting, messaging, creating groups)</td><td>Repeated breach</td></tr>
<tr><td>Temporary suspension of the account</td><td>Serious or repeated breach</td></tr>
<tr><td>Permanent termination of the account</td><td>Breaches listed in 6.1, multiple repeated breaches</td></tr>
<tr><td>Report to the competent authorities</td><td>Threat to life or safety</td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>

<h3>7.4. Statement of reasons (DSA, Article 17)</h3>
<p>If we remove your content, restrict its visibility, or suspend or terminate your account, we send you the following information by in-app notification and e-mail:</p>
<ul>
<li>which measure was taken and for how long;</li>
<li>the facts on which the decision is based;</li>
<li>if the decision was made by an automated tool, information about this;</li>
<li>the law breached or the relevant clause of the Terms;</li>
<li>the ways to appeal (7.5 and 7.6).</li>
</ul>
<p>This information may not be provided where the law prohibits it (for example, during a criminal investigation) or in the case of deceptive high-volume commercial content.</p>

<h3>7.5. Internal complaints (DSA, Article 20)</h3>
<p>Within 6 months of being informed of a decision, and also where we have taken no action on your report, you can file a complaint free of charge: in the app via Profile → Moderation history → the "Appeal this decision" button, or by writing to support@anacan.az. The complaint is reviewed not solely by an automated tool but by a different moderator who did not make the original decision. If the decision was wrong, we reverse it without delay and restore the content or the account.</p>

<h3>7.6. Out-of-court dispute settlement (DSA, Article 21)</h3>
<p>If you live in the EU and disagree with a decision, you can also refer the matter to an out-of-court dispute settlement body certified by the supervisory authority. The list is published on the European Commission's website. This option does not limit your right to go to court.</p>

<h3>7.7. Private messages</h3>
<p>We do not proactively read private messages. A moderator reviews messages only when a participant in the conversation reports them. In that case, the reported message and its immediate context are reviewed. Private messages are encrypted in transit (TLS) and when stored on our servers, but they are not end-to-end encrypted.</p>

<h3>7.8. Misuse (DSA, Article 23)</h3>
<p>We suspend, for a reasonable period and after a prior warning, the activity of accounts that frequently share manifestly illegal content. We may also temporarily suspend the ability to submit reports for those who frequently submit manifestly unfounded reports or complaints.</p>

<h3>7.9. Threat to life (DSA, Article 18)</h3>
<p>If we suspect a criminal offence involving a threat to the life or safety of a person, we promptly inform the law enforcement authorities of the country concerned.</p>

<h3>7.10. Transparency</h3>
<p>We publish a transparency report on our moderation activities once a year.</p>

<h2>8. Brand partners, advertising and external links</h2>
<p>We always show partner offers and advertisements with an "Ad" or "Partner" label. The partner is responsible for the product or service you purchase from that partner.</p>

<h3>8.1. Labelling of advertising and partner content</h3>
<ul>
<li>Every advertisement and every piece of partner content clearly shows on whose behalf the advertisement is displayed (DSA, Article 26).</li>
<li>We do not show advertising based on your health data, your children's data or your protected characteristics (religion, ethnicity, etc.).</li>
<li>Advertising based on profiling is not shown to users under 18 (DSA, Article 28(2)).</li>
<li>Articles prepared with partner sponsorship are labelled as "Partner content".</li>
</ul>

<h3>8.2. Partner offers and discounts</h3>
<ul>
<li>Discount codes and partner offers are subject to the partner's own terms: validity period, terms of use, country restrictions.</li>
<li>The contract for a product or service you purchase from a partner is concluded between you and the partner. Contact the partner on matters of quality, delivery, warranty and returns.</li>
<li>Offers from partners in the medical sector are not medical recommendations. Anacan does not recommend any medicine, medical product or clinic from a medical point of view.</li>
<li>If you have a complaint about a partner offer, write to support@anacan.az. We may end our cooperation with a partner that breaches the rules.</li>
</ul>

<h3>8.3. External links</h3>
<p>The Service may contain links to third-party websites and apps. We are not responsible for their content, security or privacy practices. These links do not mean that we recommend or endorse those parties.</p>

<h3>8.4. Paid collaborations by users</h3>
<p>Users who post in the community in exchange for money, products or other benefits from a brand must clearly label this (see 6.3).</p>

<h2>9. Anacan's intellectual property</h2>
<p>The app, its design, code, articles, illustrations, and the "Anacan" name and logo belong to Anacan or its licensors. We grant you a limited right to use the app solely for personal, non-commercial purposes.</p>

<h3>9.1. The licence granted to you</h3>
<p>For as long as you comply with these Terms, Anacan grants you a non-exclusive, non-transferable, revocable licence to download the app to your own devices and use it for personal, non-commercial purposes.</p>

<h3>9.2. What you may not do without permission</h3>
<ul>
<li>Copy, sell or distribute Anacan's articles, images and other content for commercial purposes. Sharing for personal use (for example, sending a link to an article to a friend) is permitted.</li>
<li>Modify, reverse engineer or extract the code of the app, except where expressly permitted by law.</li>
<li>Use the "Anacan" name and logo in a way that creates the impression that you are affiliated with Anacan.</li>
<li>Automatically collect the content of the Service in order to train artificial intelligence models.</li>
</ul>

<h3>9.3. Notice of intellectual property infringement</h3>
<p>If you believe that your intellectual property rights have been infringed in the community, send the following to legal@anacan.az: a description of the right, the location of the infringing content, your contact details and a confirmation that the information is accurate. The notice is reviewed in accordance with the procedure in Section 7.</p>

<h3>9.4. Feedback and suggestions</h3>
<p>We may use your feedback and suggestions about the Service without any obligation to you. This does not affect your rights to user content.</p>

<h2>10. Termination</h2>
<p>You can delete your account at any time. We, for our part, suspend or terminate your account only on the grounds set out in these Terms, stating the reason and giving you the opportunity to appeal.</p>

<h3>10.1. By you</h3>
<p>You can delete your account at any time under Profile → Settings → Privacy and Data → Delete account. Deletion is free of charge and no penalty applies. Cancel any active subscription separately in the store settings (see 4.4).</p>

<h3>10.2. By Anacan</h3>
<p>We may suspend or terminate your account only in the following cases:</p>
<ul>
<li>serious or repeated breach of these Terms (Sections 6 and 7);</li>
<li>a legal requirement or a decision of a competent authority;</li>
<li>your account posing a real danger to other users, the Service or third parties;</li>
<li>fraud, account takeover or breach of the age requirement;</li>
<li>the account not having been used for 24 months (in accordance with the Privacy Policy, with prior notice by e-mail).</li>
</ul>
<p>In these cases, we state the reason in accordance with clause 7.4 and provide the opportunity to appeal under clauses 7.5–7.6. Unless there is an urgent danger, we give a warning before permanent termination.</p>

<h3>10.3. Discontinuation of the Service</h3>
<p>If we decide to discontinue the Service entirely or any of its features, we notify you at least 60 days in advance and give you the opportunity to export your data. We will endeavour to provide a pro-rata refund for any paid but unused subscription period.</p>

<h3>10.4. Consequences of termination</h3>
<ul>
<li>After the account is closed, your data is deleted in accordance with the periods set out in the Privacy Policy.</li>
<li>If Anacan has closed your account, unless the law or security considerations prevent it, we give you 30 days to export your cycle, pregnancy and child records before deletion.</li>
<li>Copies of messages you have sent to other users may remain in their conversations.</li>
<li>Clauses which by their nature should survive termination (intellectual property, liability, governing law) remain in force.</li>
</ul>

<h2>11. Warranties and liability</h2>
