<h3>5.5. Photos of children</h3>
<p>Before sharing photos of your child in the community, think about their future privacy. Do not share nude or semi-nude photos of a child, or photos that reveal their school, address or daily route. We may remove such content in order to protect children. Sharing a photo of someone else's child without the consent of that child's parent is prohibited.</p>

<h2>6. Community rules</h2>
<p>The Anacan community is a safe and supportive space for women and parents. The following content and conduct are prohibited; depending on the severity of the breach, the measures in Section 7 are taken.</p>

<h3>6.1. Zero tolerance (immediate account termination)</h3>
<ul>
<li>Any content related to the sexual exploitation or sexualisation of children, and any attempt to establish inappropriate contact with children (grooming). Such content is reported to the competent authorities.</li>
<li>Promotion of terrorism and violent extremism.</li>
<li>Real threats of violence against a specific person.</li>
<li>Human trafficking, buying or selling of children or babies, illegal adoption or surrogacy offers.</li>
<li>Non-consensual sharing of intimate images.</li>
</ul>

<h3>6.2. Prohibited content</h3>
<ul>
<li><strong>Insults and harassment:</strong> insults, humiliation, threats and intimidation, stalking, mocking another person's body, parenting decisions or pregnancy loss.</li>
<li><strong>Hate speech:</strong> attacks based on race, ethnicity, religion, nationality, sex, disability or other protected characteristics.</li>
<li><strong>Self-harm:</strong> content that encourages or shows methods of suicide, self-harm or disordered eating. Seeking support on these topics is not prohibited; we may add support resources to such posts.</li>
<li><strong>Dangerous health misinformation:</strong> calls to refuse proven treatment, to use dangerous "treatment" methods, or to engage in practices that could harm children and pregnant women.</li>
<li><strong>Sale of medicines and medical products:</strong> offers to buy, sell or hand over prescription medicines, medicines for terminating a pregnancy, hormones, breast milk or medical devices.</li>
<li><strong>Disclosure of personal information (doxxing):</strong> sharing another person's address, phone number, workplace, health information or photos without their consent.</li>
<li><strong>Fraud and deception:</strong> scams, fake fundraising, pyramid schemes, posing as a doctor or specialist, impersonating another person.</li>
<li><strong>Sexual content:</strong> pornographic or sexually explicit content. Educational content on reproductive health and breastfeeding is not prohibited.</li>
<li><strong>Graphic violence:</strong> bloody or shocking images without a warning. Sensitive images on childbirth and medical topics may be shared only with a "sensitive content" label.</li>
<li><strong>Intellectual property infringement:</strong> sharing someone else's content without permission.</li>
<li><strong>Illegal content:</strong> other content prohibited by the law of the country where you live or by EU law.</li>
</ul>

<h3>6.3. Prohibited conduct</h3>
<ul>
<li>Spam, mass or automated messages, fake accounts, bots.</li>
<li>Undisclosed advertising: if you post in exchange for payment or gifts from a brand, you must clearly indicate this with the "#ad" or "#collaboration" tag.</li>
<li>Creating a new account to evade moderation.</li>
<li>Abuse of the reporting system (unfounded, mass complaints).</li>
<li>Interfering with the security of the Service, automated collection of data (scraping), reverse engineering the app's code (except where permitted by law).</li>
<li>Asking other users for personal information, money or intimate images outside the community.</li>
</ul>

<h3>6.4. Obligations of group administrators</h3>
<p>Users who create or manage a group:</p>
<ul>
<li>must make efforts to ensure compliance with these Terms in the group;</li>
<li>must state any additional rules clearly in the group description;</li>
<li>must clearly disclose when they direct group members to paid services outside the group;</li>
<li>must report content that breaches the rules to us.</li>
</ul>
<p>Group administrators are not employees or representatives of Anacan.</p>

<h2>7. Moderation, reporting and complaints</h2>
<p>The community is reviewed jointly by our moderators and automated tools. When we make a decision about your content, we tell you the reason, and you can appeal that decision. This section has been prepared in accordance with the EU Digital Services Act (DSA, Regulation 2022/2065).</p>

<h3>7.1. Reporting content that breaches the rules (DSA, Article 16)</h3>
<p>Anyone, including people without an account, can report illegal content or content that breaches these Terms:</p>
<ul>
<li>in the app, using the <strong>"Report"</strong> button next to a post, story, comment, group, profile or message;</li>
<li>for people without an account, via report@anacan.az.</li>
</ul>
<p>A report of illegal content must include:</p>
<ol>
<li>an explanation of why the content is illegal;</li>
<li>the exact location of the content (a link or an in-app report);</li>
<li>your name and e-mail address (except for reports concerning child sexual abuse — these may be submitted anonymously);</li>
<li>a confirmation that you believe in good faith that the information in the report is accurate.</li>
</ol>
<p>We confirm receipt of the report, review it in a timely, objective and impartial manner, and inform you of the decision.</p>

<h3>7.2. How moderation is carried out</h3>
<ul>
<li>Reports are reviewed by human moderators. Moderators are trained on health and child-related topics.</li>
<li>We use automated tools for spam, known illegal images and clear-cut rules. Decisions made by an automated tool that result in an account being terminated are reviewed by a human.</li>
<li>Feed and group recommendations are ranked by an algorithm. The main ranking parameters are: the accounts and groups you follow, your life stage, interactions and the date of the post.</li>
</ul>

<h3>7.3. Measures</h3>
<p>Depending on the severity of the breach, whether it is repeated and the context, one or more of the following measures are applied:</p>
<table>
<thead><tr><th>Measure</th><th>Example case</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
<tr><td>Warning</td><td>First-time, minor breach</td></tr>
<tr><td>Restricting the visibility of content ("sensitive content" label, removal from recommendations)</td><td>Graphic medical image</td></tr>
<tr><td>Removal of content</td><td>Insults, misinformation, sales</td></tr>
<tr><td>Temporary restriction of features (posting, messaging, creating groups)</td><td>Repeated breach</td></tr>
<tr><td>Temporary suspension of the account</td><td>Serious or repeated breach</td></tr>
<tr><td>Permanent termination of the account</td><td>Breaches listed in 6.1, multiple repeated breaches</td></tr>
<tr><td>Report to the competent authorities</td><td>Threat to life or safety</td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>

<h3>7.4. Statement of reasons (DSA, Article 17)</h3>
<p>If we remove your content, restrict its visibility, or suspend or terminate your account, we send you the following information by in-app notification and e-mail:</p>
<ul>
<li>which measure was taken and for how long;</li>
<li>the facts on which the decision is based;</li>
<li>if the decision was made by an automated tool, information about this;</li>
<li>the law breached or the relevant clause of the Terms;</li>
<li>the ways to appeal (7.5 and 7.6).</li>
</ul>
<p>This information may not be provided where the law prohibits it (for example, during a criminal investigation) or in the case of deceptive high-volume commercial content.</p>

<h3>7.5. Internal complaints (DSA, Article 20)</h3>
<p>Within 6 months of being informed of a decision, and also where we have taken no action on your report, you can file a complaint free of charge: in the app via Profile → Moderation history → the "Appeal this decision" button, or by writing to support@anacan.az. The complaint is reviewed not solely by an automated tool but by a different moderator who did not make the original decision. If the decision was wrong, we reverse it without delay and restore the content or the account.</p>

<h3>7.6. Out-of-court dispute settlement (DSA, Article 21)</h3>
<p>If you live in the EU and disagree with a decision, you can also refer the matter to an out-of-court dispute settlement body certified by the supervisory authority. The list is published on the European Commission's website. This option does not limit your right to go to court.</p>

<h3>7.7. Private messages</h3>
<p>We do not proactively read private messages. A moderator reviews messages only when a participant in the conversation reports them. In that case, the reported message and its immediate context are reviewed. Private messages are encrypted in transit (TLS) and when stored on our servers, but they are not end-to-end encrypted.</p>

<h3>7.8. Misuse (DSA, Article 23)</h3>
<p>We suspend, for a reasonable period and after a prior warning, the activity of accounts that frequently share manifestly illegal content. We may also temporarily suspend the ability to submit reports for those who frequently submit manifestly unfounded reports or complaints.</p>

<h3>7.9. Threat to life (DSA, Article 18)</h3>
<p>If we suspect a criminal offence involving a threat to the life or safety of a person, we promptly inform the law enforcement authorities of the country concerned.</p>

<h3>7.10. Transparency</h3>
<p>We publish a transparency report on our moderation activities once a year.</p>

