  content = $L$<p><strong>Effective date:</strong> 05.03.2026. <strong>Last updated:</strong> 05.03.2026. <strong>Version:</strong> 2.0.</p>

<h2>1. Introduction and data controller</h2>
<p>Your health data is never sold, never used for advertising and never passed on to advertising partners. This policy explains how we collect, use, store, share and protect your personal data in the Anacan mobile app, website and related services (together, the "Service").</p>

<h3>1.1. Who we are</h3>
<p>The operator of the Service and the controller of your personal data ("data controller", "owner and operator"):</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Legal entity:</strong> "ANACAN" Məhdud Məsuliyyətli Cəmiyyəti</li>
<li><strong>TIN / registration number:</strong> 1407578211</li>
<li><strong>Registered address:</strong> Şamil Əzizbəyov 150</li>
<li><strong>Contact for privacy matters:</strong> privacy@anacan.az</li>
<li><strong>Data Protection Officer (DPO):</strong> Jamil Sultanli, dpo@anacan.az</li>


</ul>

<h3>1.2. Scope</h3>
<p>This policy applies to everyone who uses the Service — registered users, website visitors and people who contact us. The policy does not apply to third-party websites and apps linked from the Service (for example, brand partners' shops); their own privacy policies apply.</p>

<h3>1.3. Note that we are not a medical service</h3>
<p>Anacan is not a medical device or a medical service. Cycle, ovulation and pregnancy predictions are for information only, do not replace a doctor's advice and must not be used as a method of contraception. This note does not affect how data is processed, but it clarifies the nature of the service.</p>

<h2>2. Data we collect</h2>
<p>We collect only data that is necessary to provide the Service or that you provide with your explicit consent. Data comes from three sources: what you enter yourself, what is collected automatically from your device, and what we receive from third parties.</p>
<table>
<thead><tr><th>Category</th><th>Examples</th><th>Source</th><th>Mandatory?</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
<tr><td>Account data</td><td>name or nickname, e-mail, password (in hashed form), sign-in method (Apple, Google), language, country</td><td>You</td><td>Yes, for an account</td></tr>
<tr><td>Profile data</td><td>year of birth, life stage (cycle, planning a pregnancy, pregnancy, parenthood), the goals you select</td><td>You</td><td>No</td></tr>
<tr><td>Health data</td><td>listed in detail in Section 3</td><td>You</td><td>No, with explicit consent</td></tr>
<tr><td>Child data</td><td>listed in detail in Section 4</td><td>You (the parent)</td><td>No</td></tr>
<tr><td>Subscription data</td><td>subscription type, start and end date, transaction identifier</td><td>App Store, Google Play</td><td>Yes, for Premium</td></tr>
<tr><td>Support correspondence</td><td>messages you send, screenshots, e-mail address</td><td>You</td><td>No</td></tr>
<tr><td>Community content</td><td>posts, comments and profile photo you share (where the feature is available)</td><td>You</td><td>No</td></tr>
<tr><td>Device and technical data</td><td>device model, operating system, app version, language, time zone, IP address, push notification token</td><td>Automatic</td><td>Yes</td></tr>
<tr><td>Usage and diagnostics</td><td>sections opened (without health content), session length, error and crash reports</td><td>Automatic</td><td>With consent, for analytics</td></tr>
<tr><td>Advertising data</td><td>advertising identifier (Advertising ID, IDFA), ad views and clicks</td><td>Automatic</td><td>With consent (Section 6)</td></tr>
<tr><td>Approximate location</td><td>at country and city level, from the IP address</td><td>Automatic</td><td>Yes</td></tr>
<tr><td>Partner offers</td><td>discount code you used, partner offer you clicked</td><td>You, automatic</td><td>No</td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<p><strong>Data we do not collect.</strong> We do not collect your precise GPS location, your contacts list, full access to your photo gallery (only the photo you select is uploaded), or microphone and camera data without your explicit request. We do not see or store your payment card details — store payments are processed by Apple and Google, and card payments on the website by the bank and the payment provider.</p>

<h2>3. Health data</h2>
<p>Your health data is collected only with your explicit consent, is used only to provide the service to you and can be completely deleted at any time. Under Article 9 of the GDPR, the Law of the Republic of Azerbaijan "On Personal Data" and other applicable laws, this data belongs to a special (sensitive) category and is processed with the highest level of protection.</p>

<h3>3.1. What health data we process</h3>
<p>We process the following data only when you enter it or allow it to be imported from a connected service (for example, Apple Health, Health Connect):</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Menstrual cycle:</strong> start and end dates of menstruation, flow intensity, cycle length, ovulation and fertile days (your records and our predictions).</li>
<li><strong>Symptoms and well-being:</strong> pain, mood, energy, sleep, skin, digestion, basal body temperature, cervical mucus, ovulation and pregnancy test results.</li>
<li><strong>Reproductive health:</strong> contraceptive method, pregnancy planning, sexual activity records (only if you use this feature).</li>
<li><strong>Pregnancy:</strong> estimated due date, week of pregnancy, weight, blood pressure, symptoms, doctor's visits, test records, records of pregnancy loss.</li>
<li><strong>Postpartum period:</strong> recovery, breastfeeding, postpartum mood records.</li>
<li><strong>Medicines and vitamins:</strong> name, dose, intake reminders.</li>
<li><strong>Free-form notes:</strong> health-related notes you write and documents you upload.</li>
</ul>

<h3>3.2. Legal basis: explicit consent</h3>
<p>We process health data only on the basis of your explicit, separate and voluntary consent. Consent is not hidden within the general terms of use: it is requested on a separate screen before you enter health data for the first time. You can withdraw your consent at any time under Profile → Privacy → Consent choices. When you withdraw it, new processing of health data stops and you are offered the option to delete or export the existing data. Withdrawing consent does not affect the lawfulness of processing carried out before the withdrawal.</p>

<h3>3.3. What we use health data for</h3>
<ul>
<li>to calculate cycle, ovulation and pregnancy predictions;</li>
<li>to show you relevant content, reminders and daily tips (this personalisation takes place within the app);</li>
<li>to synchronise your data across devices and keep a backup;</li>
<li>to prepare reports at your request (for example, a PDF to show your doctor).</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Product improvement.</strong> To improve our prediction algorithms, we may use health data only in aggregated or pseudonymised form that does not allow you to be identified, and only with your separate consent. This consent is not a condition for using the core service.</p>

<h3>3.4. Things we never do</h3>
<ul>
<li>We do not sell, rent or exchange your health data.</li>
<li>We do not pass your health data to advertising partners, AdMob, advertising networks or data brokers.</li>
<li>We do not use health data to target or personalise advertising — neither in our own app nor elsewhere.</li>
<li>We do not pass your health data to brand partners (including partners in the medical, pharmaceutical and insurance sectors).</li>
<li>We do not use health data for employment, credit, insurance or similar decisions, and we do not give it to anyone for such purposes.</li>
<li>We do not send event names, screen names or parameters containing health content to in-app analytics and advertising SDKs.</li>
</ul>

<h3>3.5. Storage location and protection</h3>
<p>Health data is stored on servers located in the European Union (Belgium, Google Cloud europe-west1). It is encrypted in transit with TLS 1.2+ and at rest with AES-256. The number of employees with access to health data is kept to a minimum; access is logged and granted only when necessary for technical support.</p>

<h3>3.6. Retention period</h3>
<p>Health data is kept for as long as your account is active. When you delete your account or your health data, it is permanently deleted from active systems immediately and from backups within 30 days at the latest. If an account is not used for 24 months, we delete the data after notifying you in advance by e-mail.</p>

<h3>3.7. Connected health services</h3>
<p>When you allow integration with Apple Health (HealthKit) or Google Health Connect, we read or write only the data types you select. Data obtained from HealthKit and Health Connect is not used for advertising, marketing or data sales and is not passed on to third parties. You can revoke the permission at any time in your device settings.</p>

<h2>4. Children's data and age limit</h2>
<p>Data you enter about your child is kept at the same level of protection as health data and is never used for advertising or marketing.</p>

<h3>4.1. Child data entered by the parent</h3>
<p>When you use the feature for tracking your little one's development, you can enter the following: the child's name or nickname, date of birth, sex, height and weight, feeding, sleep and nappy-change records, developmental milestones, vaccinations, illness and medication records, photos. You confirm that you enter this data only as the child's parent or legal representative.</p>
<ul>
<li>Child data is visible only in your account. When you invite another parent or caregiver to your account, they see only the child profiles you have allowed.</li>
<li>Child data is not passed to advertising partners, brand partners or any third party for marketing purposes.</li>
<li>You can separately delete a child profile or all records relating to it at any time.</li>
</ul>

<h3>4.2. Minimum age of use</h3>
<p>The minimum age for using the Service is 16. If the law of the country where you live requires a higher age, that age applies. Persons below this age may not use the Service.</p>
<p>If we discover that a user below the minimum age has created an account, we delete the account and the data relating to it. If you are aware of such a case, write to privacy@anacan.az.</p>

<h3>4.3. Restrictions for minors</h3>
<p>Users under 18 are not shown personalised advertising, their data is not used for profiling or ad targeting, and they are not sent marketing offers from brand partners. In Google AdMob requests, the relevant settings for child-directed treatment or for users under the age of consent are applied to these users.</p>

<h2>5. Purposes of data use and legal bases</h2>
<p>Our legal basis for each processing purpose is set out below. Where we process data on the basis of "legitimate interest", we balance our interests against your rights and freedoms, and you have the right to object to this processing.</p>
<table>
<thead><tr><th>Purpose</th><th>Data used</th><th>Legal basis</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
<tr><td>Creating and managing an account</td><td>account, device data</td><td>Performance of a contract</td></tr>
<tr><td>Cycle, pregnancy and child tracking features</td><td>health and child data</td><td>Explicit consent</td></tr>
<tr><td>Providing the Premium subscription</td><td>subscription data</td><td>Performance of a contract</td></tr>
<tr><td>Personalised in-app content</td><td>profile, health data</td><td>Explicit consent</td></tr>
<tr><td>Reminders and service notifications</td><td>account, push token, your settings</td><td>Performance of a contract</td></tr>
<tr><td>Marketing e-mails and notifications</td><td>e-mail, push token, profile (without health data)</td><td>Consent (opt out at any time)</td></tr>
<tr><td>Personalised advertising</td><td>advertising identifier, device and usage data (without health data)</td><td>Consent</td></tr>
<tr><td>Non-personalised advertising</td><td>device data, approximate location</td><td>Legitimate interest (funding the free service)</td></tr>
<tr><td>Showing and measuring partner offers</td><td>discount codes, clicks (without health data)</td><td>Consent</td></tr>
<tr><td>Analytics and product improvement</td><td>usage and diagnostic data</td><td>Consent</td></tr>
<tr><td>Fixing errors and ensuring stability</td><td>crash reports, device data</td><td>Legitimate interest</td></tr>
<tr><td>Security, prevention of fraud and abuse</td><td>IP address, device data, sign-in logs</td><td>Legitimate interest</td></tr>
<tr><td>Responding to support requests</td><td>support correspondence</td><td>Performance of a contract</td></tr>
<tr><td>Compliance with legal obligations (tax, accounting, court orders)</td><td>subscription, account data</td><td>Legal obligation</td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<p><strong>Automated decisions.</strong> Predictions are calculated automatically, but we do not make decisions about you based solely on automated processing that produce legal or similarly significant effects.</p>
<p><strong>Artificial intelligence features.</strong> Questions you write to the in-app assistant are sent to Google (Vertex AI, Gemini) to generate responses. This data is not used to train the provider's models. The chat history is stored in your account; you can delete it in the AI chat at any time, and it is deleted completely when you delete your account. It is your choice not to write sensitive information to the assistant.</p>

<h2>6. Advertising, Google AdMob and device identifiers</h2>
<p>We use the Google AdMob service to show advertising in the free version; the advertising system never receives your health or child data. Premium subscribers are not shown advertising.</p>

<h3>6.1. Data collected by AdMob</h3>
<p>AdMob and its advertising partners may collect and use the following to show ads, limit how often the same ad is repeated, measure ad performance, ensure security and prevent fraud:</p>
<ul>
<li>the Android advertising identifier (Advertising ID), the iOS advertising identifier (IDFA — only if you grant App Tracking Transparency permission) and similar identifiers;</li>
<li>IP address, device model, language, time zone, mobile carrier, operating system and app version;</li>
<li>ad views, clicks and ad interactions, diagnostic data;</li>
<li>approximate location (country, city) determined from the IP address.</li>
</ul>
<p>We do not use precise location for advertising.</p>

<h3>6.2. Data not passed to the advertising system</h3>
<p>The following is not passed to AdMob or other advertising partners: health data, cycle phase, pregnancy status and week, child data, your name and e-mail. Ad requests do not use keywords, contextual signals or user segments that reveal your health status or life stage. Ad placements are not shown on screens where health data is entered.</p>

<h3>6.3. Personalised and non-personalised advertising</h3>
<p>Personalised advertising is shown only with your consent and where permitted by law. For users in the European Economic Area, the United Kingdom and Switzerland, consent is obtained through a Google-certified consent management platform (CMP) in accordance with the IAB TCF standard.</p>
<p>Non-personalised or limited advertising is shown if you do not give consent or withdraw it. Such ads do not use a personal profile, but may use limited data such as device information, approximate location and ad interactions to prevent fraud and for measurement.</p>
<p>You can change your advertising choice at any time under Profile → Settings → Ad choices or Profile → Privacy → Consent choices.</p>

<h3>6.4. Your choices on iOS devices</h3>
<p>In accordance with Apple's App Tracking Transparency (ATT) rules, we ask for your permission before accessing the IDFA. Not granting permission does not restrict any feature of the app. You can change your choice at any time in your iPhone's Settings → Privacy and Security → Tracking.</p>

<h3>6.5. Your choices on Android devices</h3>
<p>Depending on your Android version, you can reset or delete your advertising identifier under Settings → Privacy → Ads (or Settings → Google → Ads). Once deleted, apps receive a value consisting of zeros instead of the identifier. Menu names may differ depending on the device manufacturer.</p>

<h3>6.6. Google's role</h3>
<p>Google processes advertising data in accordance with its own privacy policy and, in some cases, as an independent controller. More information:</p>
<ul>
<li><a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy">Google Privacy Policy</a></li>
<li><a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites">How Google uses information from sites or apps that use its services</a></li>
<li><a href="https://support.google.com/admob/answer/9012903">List of Google ad technology providers</a></li>
<li><a href="https://myadcenter.google.com/">Google My Ad Center</a></li>
</ul>

<h2>7. Brand partners and third parties</h2>
<p>We share your data only in the cases set out below and only to the extent necessary; health and child data is passed only to technical providers that provide the service to you (for example, hosting), and only on condition that they process it solely on our behalf.</p>

<h3>7.1. Brand partners</h3>
<p>Anacan works with brands in the retail, medical, FMCG, wellness, education and services sectors: partner discounts, in-app banners, articles and e-commerce offers.</p>
<ul>
<li>Partner content is shown with an "Ad" or "Partner" label.</li>
<li>Partners do not receive your name, e-mail, health or child data.</li>
<li>We share only aggregated, anonymous statistics with partners (for example, "the banner was shown 1,200 times and received 85 clicks").</li>
<li>When you use a discount code or go to a partner's website, the partner receives only the data you give it directly and processes it in accordance with its own privacy policy.</li>
<li>If partner offers are shown based on life stage (for example, "pregnancy" or "parent of a baby"), this selection takes place only within the app and the targeting data is not passed to the partner.</li>
</ul>

<h3>7.2. Service providers (processors)</h3>
<p>Providers that process data on our behalf and under a written contract. They may not use your data for their own purposes.</p>
<table>
<thead><tr><th>Provider category</th><th>Service</th><th>Purpose</th><th>Do they receive health data?</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
<tr><td>Cloud hosting and database</td><td>Google Cloud (Belgium)</td><td>Data storage</td><td>Yes, in encrypted form</td></tr>
<tr><td>Authentication</td><td>Anacan servers, Sign in with Apple, Sign in with Google</td><td>Account sign-in</td><td>No</td></tr>
<tr><td>Analytics (with consent only)</td><td>Google Firebase Analytics; Meta App Events (ad measurement)</td><td>Usage statistics</td><td>No</td></tr>
<tr><td>Push notifications</td><td>Firebase Cloud Messaging, Apple Push Notification service</td><td>Sending notifications</td><td>No (notification text is kept generic)</td></tr>
<tr><td>E-mail delivery</td><td>Customer.io</td><td>Service and marketing e-mails</td><td>No</td></tr>
<tr><td>Subscription management</td><td>RevenueCat, App Store, Google Play</td><td>Payment verification</td><td>No</td></tr>
<tr><td>Card payments (website)</td><td>Epoint (bank payment page)</td><td>Payments for subscriptions, books and cakes on the website</td><td>No</td></tr>
<tr><td>Artificial intelligence</td><td>Google Vertex AI (Gemini)</td><td>AI assistant responses</td><td>Only if you write it to the assistant yourself</td></tr>
<tr><td>Translation</td><td>Anthropic, Microsoft Azure OpenAI</td><td>Translation of community posts</td><td>Only if you write it in a post yourself</td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<p><strong>Notification texts.</strong> In notifications shown on the lock screen, we do not display text revealing pregnancy, cycle or other health information, unless you have separately chosen this in the settings.</p>

<h3>7.3. Independent controllers</h3>
<p>Google (AdMob), Apple and Google Play process some data as independent controllers in accordance with their own rules.</p>

<h3>7.4. Other cases of sharing</h3>
<ul>
<li><strong>Legal requirements:</strong> only in the manner described in Section 9.</li>
<li><strong>Merger or sale of the company:</strong> data may pass to a new owner only on condition that the obligations in this policy are complied with; we notify you in advance, and new consent is required for health data.</li>
<li><strong>At your request:</strong> for example, when you send a report to your doctor or your partner.</li>
</ul>

<h3>7.5. Sale of data</h3>
<p>We do not sell your personal data for money or other valuable consideration. Under the laws of some US states (for example, the California CCPA/CPRA), sharing advertising identifiers with advertising networks may be considered a "sale" or "sharing for cross-context behavioural advertising". To opt out of this in respect of advertising data passed to AdMob in this sense, write to privacy@anacan.az. We also honour the Global Privacy Control (GPC) signal as an opt-out.</p>

<h2>8. Storage location, international transfers and retention periods</h2>
<p>Your data is stored on servers in the European Union (Belgium, Google Cloud europe-west1) and is transferred to another country only where lawful safeguards are in place.</p>

<h3>8.1. Storage location</h3>
<ul>
<li>Main database (account, health and child data): European Union (Belgium, Google Cloud europe-west1).</li>
<li>Analytics, crash reports, advertising data: the providers' servers, including in the USA.</li>
<li>Backups: European Union (Belgium, Google Cloud europe-west1), in encrypted form.</li>
</ul>
<p>Where Azerbaijani legislation requires certain types of personal data to be stored within the country, we comply with that requirement.</p>

<h3>8.2. International transfers</h3>
<p>When data is transferred outside the country where you live, we apply one of the following safeguards:</p>
<ul>
<li>an adequacy decision of the European Commission (for example, transfers to companies certified under the EU–US Data Privacy Framework);</li>
<li>the European Commission's Standard Contractual Clauses (SCCs) and, for the United Kingdom, the International Data Transfer Addendum;</li>
<li>in accordance with Azerbaijani legislation, transfers to countries that ensure an adequate level of protection, or your consent;</li>
<li>a transfer risk assessment and additional technical measures (encryption, pseudonymisation).</li>
</ul>
<p>You can request a copy of the safeguards from privacy@anacan.az.</p>

<h3>8.3. Retention periods</h3>
<table>
<thead><tr><th>Data type</th><th>Retention period</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
<tr><td>Account data</td><td>For as long as the account is active; deleted within 30 days after deletion of the account</td></tr>
<tr><td>Health and child data</td><td>For as long as the account is active or until you delete it; deleted from backups within 30 days</td></tr>
<tr><td>Inactive accounts</td><td>If not used for 24 months, deleted 30 days after a warning</td></tr>
<tr><td>Subscription and transaction records</td><td>The period required by tax and accounting legislation (5 years)</td></tr>
<tr><td>Support correspondence</td><td>24 months after the request is closed</td></tr>
<tr><td>Analytics data</td><td>A maximum of 14 months, then anonymised or deleted</td></tr>
<tr><td>Crash reports</td><td>90 days</td></tr>
<tr><td>Security and sign-in logs</td><td>12 months</td></tr>
<tr><td>Consent records (when and to what you consented)</td><td>For as long as the consent is in force and 3 years after it is withdrawn (for evidential purposes)</td></tr>
<tr><td>Advertising data</td><td>In accordance with Google's retention rules</td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>

<h3>8.4. Deleting your account</h3>
<p>You can delete your account in the app under Profile → Settings → Privacy and Data → Delete account, or by writing to privacy@anacan.az. You are given the opportunity to export your data before deletion. Deletion cannot be undone. An App Store or Google Play subscription is not automatically cancelled when the account is deleted — you must cancel it separately in the store settings.</p>

<h2>9. Security, breach notification and requests from public authorities</h2>
<p>We protect your data with technical and organisational measures, and we disclose your health data only on the basis of a valid court order and to the minimum extent necessary.</p>

<h3>9.1. Security measures</h3>
<ul>
<li>encryption in transit with TLS 1.2 or higher;</li>
<li>encryption at rest with AES-256; encryption keys are managed separately;</li>
<li>role-based access control, two-factor authentication for employees, logging of access;</li>
<li>restriction of access to health data on a "need-to-know" basis;</li>
<li>confidentiality obligations for employees and contractors;</li>
<li>regular security audits and vulnerability testing;</li>
<li>strong password requirements for your account.</li>
</ul>
<p>No system is completely secure. Do not share your password with anyone and keep your device locked.</p>

<h3>9.2. Data breaches</h3>
<p>If a security incident affecting your personal data occurs:</p>
<ul>
<li>we notify the supervisory authority where required by applicable law (under the GDPR, within 72 hours of becoming aware of the incident);</li>
<li>where there is a high risk to your rights and freedoms, we notify you without undue delay by e-mail or in-app notification;</li>
<li>in the case of breaches involving health data, US users are notified in accordance with the FTC Health Breach Notification Rule.</li>
</ul>

<h3>9.3. Requests from public authorities and law enforcement</h3>
<p>We disclose personal data to public authorities only when required by law. In doing so:</p>
<ul>
<li>we verify the legal basis and jurisdiction of each request;</li>
<li>we disclose health and reproductive health data only on the basis of a valid court order, and we challenge unfounded, overly broad or unlawful requests through legal channels;</li>
<li>we provide only the minimum data required;</li>
<li>unless prohibited by law, we notify you before disclosure;</li>
<li>we publish a transparency report once a year.</li>
</ul>
<p>Where there is an immediate threat to your life or the life of another person, we may make an emergency disclosure to the extent permitted by law.</p>

<h2>10. Your rights, region-specific provisions and other terms</h2>
<p>You are in control of your data: you can exercise most rights directly in the app, and the rest by writing to privacy@anacan.az, within 30 days at the latest.</p>

<h3>10.1. Your rights</h3>
<table>
<thead><tr><th>Right</th><th>What it means</th><th>How to exercise it</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
<tr><td>Access</td><td>To find out what data is stored about you and obtain a copy of it</td><td>Profile → Settings → Data export</td></tr>
<tr><td>Rectification</td><td>To correct inaccurate or incomplete data</td><td>The profile and records can be edited directly</td></tr>
<tr><td>Erasure</td><td>Deletion of data or of the account</td><td>Profile → Settings → Privacy and Data → Delete account</td></tr>
<tr><td>Portability</td><td>To receive data in a machine-readable format (JSON, CSV)</td><td>Profile → Settings → Data export</td></tr>
<tr><td>Withdrawal of consent</td><td>To revoke consent for health data, advertising, analytics or marketing</td><td>Profile → Privacy → Consent choices</td></tr>
<tr><td>Objection</td><td>To object to processing based on legitimate interest</td><td>privacy@anacan.az</td></tr>
