<p>We respond to your request within 30 days; in complex cases, this period may be extended to the extent permitted by law, and we will inform you of this. For requests that do not come from your account, we may ask for additional information to verify your identity. We do not discriminate against you for exercising your rights. You may submit a request through an authorised agent; in that case, a written authorisation is required. If we refuse your request, in the relevant US states you have the right to appeal the decision.</p>

<h3>10.2. Region-specific provisions</h3>
<p><strong>Republic of Azerbaijan.</strong> Data is processed in accordance with the Law "On Personal Data". Special categories of data (including health data) are processed only with your consent given in writing or confirmed by an electronic signature.</p>
<p><strong>European Economic Area, United Kingdom and Switzerland.</strong> All your rights under the GDPR and the UK GDPR are set out in clause 10.1.</p>
<p><strong>United States of America.</strong> Under the laws of California (CCPA/CPRA), Virginia, Colorado, Connecticut, Texas and other states, you have the rights of access, deletion, correction and portability, the right to opt out of sale and sharing, and the right to limit the use of sensitive data. Under Washington State's My Health My Data Act and a similar law in Nevada, we obtain separate consent for the collection and sharing of consumer health data, and we do not sell health data. The categories of data we have collected in the last 12 months are set out in Sections 2 and 3.</p>
<p><strong>Middle East, North Africa and Central Asia.</strong> We comply with additional rights and obligations required by local laws, such as Saudi Arabia's PDPL, the UAE's PDPL and the personal data laws of Kazakhstan and Uzbekistan (for example, local data storage, consent for transfers outside the country).</p>

<h3>10.3. Complaints to a supervisory authority</h3>
<p>We ask that you send your complaint to us first so that we can resolve the issue quickly. In addition, you have the right to lodge a complaint directly with the data protection supervisory authority of the country where you live (in Azerbaijan — the competent public authority in the field of personal data; in the EU — the Data Protection Authority of the country where you live; in the United Kingdom — the ICO).</p>

<h3>10.4. Changes to this policy</h3>
<p>We update this policy when legislation or our services change. We give notice of material changes at least 30 days before they take effect by in-app notification or e-mail. If a change involves using health data for a new purpose, we obtain your new consent. You can request previous versions from privacy@anacan.az.</p>

<h3>10.5. Language versions</h3>
<p>This policy is provided in all languages supported by the app. In the event of a conflict between language versions, the Azerbaijani text prevails, unless the law of the country where you live requires otherwise.</p>

